Title: F2-M07 — The Glass Orchard (briefing)
Credit: Staalfront
Author: Staalfront narrative team
Draft date: 2026-10-17

> FADE IN:

INT. ABANDONED PACKING SHED, SOUTH GATE - FIRST LIGHT

[[AMBIENCE: wind through broken greenhouse glass, a truck ticking as it cools, crows]]
[[MUSIC: thin, high tension]]

An old irrigation survey of the research complex is unrolled on a crate. COMMANDER SAVA and LENKA stand over it. Lenka's files are in a waterproof sleeve.

LENKA
(analytical)
The analysts inside the orchard decoded a repeating command phrase. They believe it links the forged orders to a single source.

LENKA
Belief is not proof. The intercept rig in the seed store is still recording. If the phrase arrives on both sides of the line while it runs, that is a pattern, and a pattern we can show to Command.

[[SHOT: map]]
[[MAP: walled orchard with south gate, south lane covered by a tower, mid lane, greenhouses with sniper, shelter and seed store in the north-west corner, tree rows west, irrigation channels drawn as faint dotted lines]]

COMMANDER SAVA
(measured)
The complex is full of blind corners and old irrigation channels. A direct assault could bury the evidence.

COMMANDER SAVA
(clipped)
Seventeen of us and one truck. No base, no reserve. The risk is not the garrison; it is that the Compact scouts keep appearing behind our people and I cannot see how.

LENKA
Three analysts, one rig. The rig cannot be moved. The analysts can, slowly, and they will be the target the moment we have them.

COMMANDER SAVA
(serious)
Medics in the middle. Civilians in the middle. Nothing touches that rig while it is still recording.

LENKA
(firm)
Reach the analysts, escort them out, and preserve the transmission equipment.

COMMANDER SAVA
(quieter)
And look at the ground, not just the hedges. Something in this orchard is older than the map.

[[SFX: radio click]]
[[MUSIC: stop]]

> FADE OUT.
